{
  "rule_2c": "A matched positive control passes the counterfactual audit if its target concept has the largest effect, positive and significant (two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank test on per-trajectory slopes, BH-corrected p < 0.05, median slope > 0), in at least 3 of 4 bases. It passes TCAV if its target concept has the highest mean TCAV score (ties broken by the mean cosine of gradient and CAV), differs from random CAVs (Welch t-test, BH-corrected within the 7 concepts, p < 0.05) and is above them, in at least 6 of 8 settings (2 layers x 2 ISIC concept-set variants x 2 input sets). Fixed before the Phase 2c run.",
  "rule_2d": "Each concept (pigment network, vascular structures, pigmentation, regression structures) has 4 matched controls: ResNet-50 seeds 1, 2, 3 and ViT-B/16 seed 1 (the seed-1 ResNet-50 controls for the first three concepts are those of Phase 2c). Regression uses high = pseudo-label >= 0.5 and caliper 1.0 because the label is sparse; the other concepts use the Phase 2c groups. A control passes as in the Phase 2c rule. The audit is valid for a concept if at least 3 of its 4 controls pass; the same count is reported for TCAV. Captum TCAV: the Phase 2b rule and the Phase 2c matched-control rule on the 4 settings available (late layer x 2 ISIC concept-set types x 2 input sets; at least 3 of 4). Fixed before the Phase 2d run; earlier verdicts are not changed.",
